    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">September, 1888. The shadow of the Whitechapel Murderer looms over London.</h2><br>Eddy Nichols, the eldest son of the first acknowledged victim, arrives at Whitechapel in search of answers. What he finds, though, is a panic-stricken city and a number of people eager to make the most of the horrible crimes: an American private eye, thirsty for fame and glory; the owner of an awful tabloid; a psychiatrist who advocates for suspicious, questionable methods, and an elusive, mentally unstable journalist.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Experience the investigation surrounding the Jack the Ripper crimes putting yourself on the shoes of one of the protagonists in this thrilling mystery Visual Novel!:</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Around 35k words of mystery and romance.<br></li><li>Two (optional) LGBT love interests.<br></li><li>Three suspects.<br></li><li>Three endings, depending on your choices.<br></li><li>A gripping original soundtrack.<br></li><li>Rating 15+</li></ul> <br><strong>DISCLAIMERS:</strong> <i>This story is based on well-known true facts, and most of the characters are inspired by real people. However, their personality and actions during the Whitechapel crimes are mostly just fiction.<br><br>The deprecating statements about England were a common opinion among the working class of Victorian Britain, and by no means represent the opinion of the writer.</i><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">The team:</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Project leader and script: Ertal<br></li><li>Characters design: Cube<br></li><li>Backgrounds: Fuyunokawa<br></li><li>CG illustrations: Pumpkin-spike<br></li><li>Music: Fricochet<br></li><li>GUI: Re. Alice</li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">September, 1888. The shadow of the Whitechapel Murderer looms over London.</h2><br>Eddy Nichols, the eldest son of the first acknowledged victim, arrives at Whitechapel in search of answers. What he finds, though, is a panic-stricken city and a number of people eager to make the most of the horrible crimes: an American private eye, thirsty for fame and glory; the owner of an awful tabloid; a psychiatrist who advocates for suspicious, questionable methods, and an elusive, mentally unstable journalist.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Experience the investigation surrounding the Jack the Ripper crimes putting yourself on the shoes of one of the protagonists in this thrilling mystery Visual Novel!:</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Around 35k words of mystery and romance.<br></li><li>Two (optional) LGBT love interests.<br></li><li>Three suspects.<br></li><li>Three endings, depending on your choices.<br></li><li>A gripping original soundtrack.<br></li><li>Rating 15+</li></ul> <br><strong>DISCLAIMERS:</strong> <i>This story is based on well-known true facts, and most of the characters are inspired by real people. However, their personality and actions during the Whitechapel crimes are mostly just fiction.<br><br>The deprecating statements about England were a common opinion among the working class of Victorian Britain, and by no means represent the opinion of the writer.</i><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">The team:</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Project leader and script: Ertal<br></li><li>Characters design: Cube<br></li><li>Backgrounds: Fuyunokawa<br></li><li>CG illustrations: Pumpkin-spike<br></li><li>Music: Fricochet<br></li><li>GUI: Re. Alice</li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Chasing Jack the Ripper! A BL/ Yaoi Visual Novel",
